{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:79940a5d4b9f0ebf","name":"Sandcrawler","source":{"id":"source:reference-79940a5d4b9f0ebf","title":"Sandcrawler","revision":21736,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T02:22:59Z","sha256":"b4d1d633892214b1c9d90c6e1fa66ed5b6b1c7798f5f28e3af9682ffc2a501fd","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21736","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Sandcrawler&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-79940a5d4b9f0ebf","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Web Enhancements"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Web_Enhancements"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Czerka Corporation Multi-Environment Tracked Transport (M-ETT)- colloquially referred to as a \"Sandcrawler\"- is designed for environments where repulsorcraft are too difficult or expensive to use. The M-ETT functions well in a variety of terrain, but it excels on dry, arid worlds (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"},") where the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tracked Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tracked_Vehicle"}," can find purchase on unstable ground. The rolling sand dunes of desert worlds make using ",{"tag":"a","children":["Walkers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Walkers","referenceId":"reference:552672704065a9f2"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wheeled Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wheeled_Vehicles","referenceId":"reference:a8a2bcfe030d4367"}," difficult, and sandstorms and fine airborne particles can cause malfunctions in repulsorlifts.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One of the most sophisticated ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ground Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ground_Vehicles"}," on the market, the M-ETT is an extremely large transport capable of hauling enough supplies to sustain it's crew for an extended time in the blazing desert. Its extensive cargo space allows it to store resources in such quantities that the Sandcrawler need make only infrequent trips to settlements. The interior of the Sandcrawler is climate controlled, allowing the crew to escape from harsh environmental conditions.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Sandcrawler Statistics (CL 3)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tracked Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tracked_Vehicle"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -7; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 13 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 26; +15 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 250; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 15; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 76\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 4 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Character_Scale"},"); (Maximum Velocity 40 km/h)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"